# Netlify redirect rules for the published site. build.sh copies this into dist/.
#
# Short link for outreach: the standalone demo is the primary "Live Demo" target
# (see README.md), and <your-domain>/demo is what fits in an email. A 301 rather
# than a rewrite so the address bar ends on the canonical URL that the page's
# own <link rel="canonical"> already declares — a rewrite would serve the same
# content at two addresses and split the signal.
/demo    /demo-standalone.html    301

# www -> apex is NOT set here on purpose. Netlify does that itself once a
# primary domain is chosen in Domain settings, and hardcoding one direction
# would fight that setting (and loop) if the other is picked.

# The assessor page was /3pao.html until the buyer-facing rename to
# "Independent Assessment Services". Anything already linking the old path —
# outreach emails, a partner's site, a search result — has to keep landing.
/3pao.html    /assessors.html    301
